      "writtenOn": "2022-10-07T16:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, that gets into asking what a \"line\" is (and why Shaper doesn\u0027t handle formatting). It depends on if you interpret `\\r` as a \"line break\" or \"end of line\". I usually read it as a \"line break\" implying that there is a new line after it (even if empty). If it just means \"end of line\" then there is no new line until there is further content. What I see here is\n\nline 1 \"\"\n`\\r`\nline 2 \"\"\n`\\r`\nline 3 \"\"\n`\\r`\nline 4 \"foo\"\n`\\r`\nline 5 \"\"\n`\\r`\nline 6 \"\"\n\nIf it isn\u0027t interpreted this way then it seems rather awkward to have a last empty line if one wants one. It means adding a `\\r\\r` at the end to get one empty line to force the actual last line (or penultimate line?) to be \"non-empty\" by virtue of being \"ended\" by the actual final `\\r`.",
      "parentUuid": "32d50b81_bc44e1ed",
      "revId": "aae771729ddaaca0bbab954c25886e6bfcba1dd6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
